-- title:
--   Base change of function fields: generation and linear disjointness
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $K$ be fields with $K$ a $k$-algebra, let $Y$ be an integral scheme equipped with a morphism $g : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, and form the fibre product $Y_K = Y \times_{\operatorname{Spec} k} \operatorname{Spec} K$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $k \to K$, assumed integral as well. Write $\mathrm{pr}_1, \mathrm{pr}_2$ for the two projections, and for a morphism $c$ from an integral scheme $C$ to $\operatorname{Spec} F$ let $\mathrm{baseToFunctionField}\ c : F \to \mathcal{O}_{C,\xi_C}$ be the ring map obtained from $c$ on global sections followed by taking germs at the generic point $\xi_C$, so that the function field of $C$ is an $F$-algebra. Let $\mathrm{prStar} : K(Y) \to K(Y_K)$ be a ring homomorphism satisfying: for every open $U \subseteq Y$ containing $\xi_Y$, every proof that $\xi_{Y_K} \in \mathrm{pr}_1^{-1}U$, and every section $s \in \mathcal{O}_Y(U)$, $\mathrm{prStar}$ sends the germ of $s$ at $\xi_Y$ to the germ at $\xi_{Y_K}$ of the pullback $\mathrm{pr}_1^{\#}s$. Then two things hold: first, the subfield of $K(Y_K)$ generated by the union of the image of $K \to K(Y_K)$ (via $\mathrm{pr}_2$) and the image of $\mathrm{prStar}$ is all of $K(Y_K)$; second, for every finite subset $t \subseteq K(Y)$ whose elements are linearly independent over $k$ — in the form that any family $c : t \to k$ with $\sum_x \mathrm{baseToFunctionField}\ g\,(c\,x)\cdot x = 0$ vanishes identically — and every family $c : t \to K$ with $\sum_x \mathrm{baseToFunctionField}\ \mathrm{pr}_2\,(c\,x)\cdot \mathrm{prStar}(x) = 0$, one has $c\,x = 0$ for all $x \in t$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that for an integral scheme $Y$ over $k$ with integral base change $Y_K$, the function field $K(Y_K)$ is generated by $K$ together with the pullback of $K(Y)$, and that $K(Y)$ and $K$ are linearly disjoint over $k$ inside $K(Y_K)$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development, where a curve over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ is compared with its base change to a completion, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_germ_eq_of_curveModel_of_iso_pullback_completion`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_germ_eq_of_curveModel_of_iso_pullback_completion).
